{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And not. Naval.</b> From the root of נובלת עליה (Isaiah 1:30)." "<b>Kilay.</b> The opposite of שוע and שוע, like נדיב whose hands are slack to give and not closed, from the root of ושוע אל ההר (Isaiah 22:5). And there is, by way of derash, that the word כילי is two words: כי יאמר שלי שלי (Avot 5:13)."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:56:17.088350217Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}